<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kanoman Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1677 CE – 1815 CE (approx.) · capital Cirebon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Junior branch of the divided Cirebon Sultanate, ruled by the Sultan Anom from a palace in the heart of old Cirebon.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kanoman was created in 1677 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-ageng-tirtayasa">Sultan Ageng Tirtayasa</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banten-sultanate">Banten Sultanate</a> partitioned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a> among the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panembahan-girilaya">Panembahan Girilaya</a>, who had died as a hostage of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mataram-sultanate">Mataram</a>. The younger son, Pangeran Kartawijaya, became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Anom, the junior sultan, alongside his elder brother in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kasepuhan-sultanate">Kasepuhan Sultanate</a>, and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keraton-kanoman">Keraton Kanoman</a> as his seat.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The two sultans shared authority over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a>, a port and pilgrimage centre around the grave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunan-gunung-jati">Sunan Gunung Jati</a>, and rivalry between their houses invited outside arbitration. From 1681 both accepted the protection of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-east-india-company-territories">Dutch East India Company</a>, which controlled their trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indigo">indigo</a> and textiles. A further split in 1807 created the Kacirebonan line.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Reforms under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herman-willem-daendels">Herman Willem Daendels</a> and the British during <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-java">British Java</a> removed the sultans political powers by 1815, leaving them pensions and ceremonial roles. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keraton-kanoman">Keraton Kanoman</a> survives, still hosting traditional rites and markets.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1677 CE – 1815 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.07%;width:2.75%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1677 CE – 1815 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cirebon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kartawijaya (Sultan Anom I)</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Javanese (Cirebon)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kanoman</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1746&amp;focus=kanoman-sultanate" aria-label="Kanoman Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7685 2430 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kanoman Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8005 2686L8005 2686M8005 2686L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8005 2686h0M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8005 2686h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8005 2686h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cirebon. <a href="/atlas?year=1746&amp;focus=kanoman-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
